#: ../../book/index.rst:1
msgid ""
"Impact of Export Controls on the Future of Open Source AI: how software, "
"model weights, and silicon hardware gates reshape human progress, proven "
"with primary sources and game theory."
msgstr "出口管制对开源人工智能未来的影响：以中美一手官方文献与通俗博弈论，揭示软件、模型权重与硅基硬件闸门如何重塑人类进步。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:5
msgid "Impact of Export Controls on the Future of Open Source AI"
msgstr "出口管制对开源人工智能未来的影响"

#: ../../book/index.rst:8
msgid ""
"Imagine a world with no tollbooths on human thought. Two centuries ago, "
"Thomas Jefferson marveled at a peculiarity of the human mind that no "
"customs officer could quite grasp: *\"He who receives an idea from me, "
"receives instruction himself without lessening mine; as he who lights his "
"taper at mine, receives light without darkening me.\"* Give away a loaf "
"of bread and your table has one loaf fewer; give away an equation and two "
"kitchens can bake tomorrow."
msgstr ""
"不妨想象一个思想无需缴纳过路费的世界。两百年前，托马斯·杰斐逊曾惊叹于人类心智中一种令任何海关官员都难以捉摸的奇妙秉性： "
"*“从我这里获得一种思想的人，自己得到了教益，却丝毫未减损我的智慧；正如借我烛火点亮他烛之人，自己获得了光明，却分毫未使我暗淡。”* "
"送出一只面包，你的餐桌上便少了一只面包；但送出一道方程，明天两间厨房都能烤出温热的新粮。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:13
msgid ""
"From an open commons to a guarded horizon: ideas once sailed freely "
"across borders like folded paper birds, before export walls rose across "
"both silicon hardware and frontier models, leaving one narrow jade "
"doorway ajar for open-source science."
msgstr ""
"从开放公地到设防的地平线：思想曾如折纸飞鸟般自由越过山海，直到出口高墙在硅基硬件与前沿大模型之间同时耸立，唯余一扇微启的碧玉窄门，仍为开源科学留出一线天光。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:15
msgid ""
"For four hundred years, humanity's greatest leaps rested on that quiet "
"miracle. Movable type, germ theory, astronomical tables, the internet "
"protocol suite, Linux, and most recently **open-source artificial "
"intelligence** flourished because strangers across oceans could read, "
"test, repair, and improve one another's work without waiting in line for "
"a sovereign export stamp. Between 2023 and 2026, open-weight models "
"turned what might have become a closed corporate priesthood into a living "
"global commons. A rural clinic in Kenya triaging childhood pneumonia "
"offline, a linguist rescuing an endangered mother tongue, and university "
"students with two consumer graphics cards in Munich or Bengaluru suddenly "
"held genuine frontier reasoning in their own hands ``[OSI]`` ``[R1]`` "
"``[QWEN]``."
msgstr ""
"四百年来，人类最伟大的每一次跃迁，都建立在这桩静默的奇迹之上。活字印刷、细菌学说、天文星表、互联网协议簇、Linux 操作系统，直至晚近崛起的 "
"**开源人工智能** "
"，之所以能够蔚然成林，正是因为隔海相望的陌生人可以自由阅读、检验、修补并精进彼此的心血，而无需排起长队等候一枚主权国家的出口印章。2023 至 "
"2026 "
"年间，开放权重模型将原本可能沦为少数科技巨头封闭秘教的技术，化作了一片生机勃勃的全球知识公地。肯尼亚离线分诊儿童肺炎的乡村诊所、抢救濒危母语的语言学家，以及慕尼黑或班加罗尔仅凭两张消费级显卡钻研的大学生，骤然间都在自己掌中握住了真正的前沿推理之力 "
"``[OSI]`` ``[R1]`` ``[QWEN]`` 。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:17
msgid ""
"Then the walls began to rise: not only in the sky of software, but deep "
"underground in the bedrock of silicon."
msgstr "随后，高墙开始拔地而起：不仅横亘在软件的苍穹之上，更深扎进地底硅基的岩床之中。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:19
msgid "Not Just Software or Weights: The Hardware Beneath Open Minds"
msgstr "不止于软件与权重：托起开放心智的硬件底座"

#: ../../book/index.rst:22
msgid ""
"Most conversations about open-source AI make a comforting mistake. They "
"imagine an AI model as pure, weightless poetry: a file of code and "
"numbers that can stay free forever as long as someone places an MIT or "
"Apache 2.0 license on GitHub."
msgstr ""
"绝大多数关于开源人工智能的讨论，都怀着一种令人宽慰的错觉。人们习惯把人工智能模型想象成纯粹而失重的诗篇：仿佛只要有人在 GitHub 上挂一份 "
"MIT 或 Apache 2.0 许可证，那一串代码与数字便能永远自由。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:24
msgid ""
"In physical reality, no neural network floats in thin air. Every open "
"model sits atop an industrial pyramid of **extreme-ultraviolet "
"lithography lenses, silicon wafers, stacked high-bandwidth memory (HBM), "
"custom processor instruction sets, and miles of optical fiber stitching "
"ten thousand accelerator cards into a single supercomputer**. Export "
"controls have now clamped onto **both halves of that stack** at once:"
msgstr ""
"然而在物理现实中，没有任何神经网络能凭空悬浮。每一座开源模型的脚下，都托举着一座庞大精密的现代工业金字塔： "
"**极紫外光刻机的光学镜头、高纯硅晶圆、层层堆叠的高带宽存储器（HBM）、定制处理器指令集，以及绵延数英里、将上万张算力加速卡缝合成一台超级计算机的高速光纤** "
"。如今，出口管制的钳口正同时咬合在这座技术栈的 **上下两半** 之上："

#: ../../book/index.rst:29
msgid ""
"Mind and silicon are inseparable: open-source constellations illuminating "
"clinics, classrooms, and workshops above ground draw their life from "
"subterranean silicon wafers, stacked HBM memory, and ten-thousand-card "
"supercluster cables now guarded by border gates."
msgstr ""
"心智与硅基密不可分：地上照亮诊所、课堂与工坊的开源星群，其生命力皆源自地底深处的硅晶圆、堆叠式 HBM "
"存储器与万卡超算集群光缆；而如今，这些地底脉络已处处设有边境关闸。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:31
msgid ""
"**Below the surface (Hardware & Silicon Chokepoints):** Washington built "
"its border fortress around physical computation, restricting flagship AI "
"chips (``3A090``), semiconductor manufacturing tools, and foreign-made "
"chips designed with US software (``15 CFR 734.9``), even after "
"calibrating conditional case-by-case review for H200-class exports in "
"January 2026 ``[US26]`` ``[EAR734]`` ``[EAR742]`` ``[EAR774]``. Beijing's "
"October 2026 draft answers in kind on the architectural side, proposing "
"export controls on **AI processor designs, custom instruction sets, IP "
"cores, 2.5D/3D chiplet packaging, non-von-Neumann chips, high-density 3D "
"NAND, and <=18 nm or stacked DRAM designs** (``266506X``), alongside "
"**10,000-card supercluster interconnects and multi-vendor "
"chip-orchestration stacks** (``266507X``) and 18 classes of solar factory "
"machinery ``[CN-A1]``."
msgstr ""
"**地平线之下（硬件与硅基咽喉要道）：** 华盛顿围绕物理算力筑起了边境要塞，严格管制旗舰级 AI 芯片（ ``3A090`` "
"）、半导体制造设备，以及凭借“外国直接产品规则”（ ``15 CFR 734.9`` ）纳入管辖、采用美国软件设计的境外制造芯片；即便在 2026 "
"年 1 月对 H200 级别芯片出口校准为附严苛条件的逐案审查后，藩篱依然森严 ``[US26]`` ``[EAR734]`` "
"``[EAR742]`` ``[EAR774]`` 。北京在 2026 年 10 月公布的目录修订草案中则从底层架构端予以回应，拟对 **AI "
"处理器架构设计、定制指令集、核心计算 IP 核、2.5D/3D 芯粒（Chiplet）先进封装、非冯·诺依曼架构芯片、高密度 3D NAND "
"闪存，以及 <=18 纳米或堆叠式 DRAM 存储芯片设计** （ ``266506X`` ）实施出口限制，并同步纳管 "
"**超万卡智算集群高速互联与多厂商异构芯片混训调度技术** （ ``266507X`` ）以及 18 类核心光伏制造装备 ``[CN-A1]`` 。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:32
msgid ""
"**Above the surface (Software, Weights & Data Gates):** On **16 October "
"2026**, China's Ministry of Commerce (MOFCOM) and Ministry of Science and "
"Technology (MOST) issued **Announcement No. 48 of 2026**, proposing **40 "
"technology checkpoints** across AI and chips (23), biomedicine (5), and "
"solar manufacturing (12) while switching on mandatory pre-export "
"registration that same afternoon ``[CN48]`` ``[CNQA]``. Private transfers "
"of frontier model weights crossing :math:`10^{26}` FLOPs, **2 trillion "
"parameters**, or a **Global Top-10 benchmark** (``266504X``) enter "
"licensing gates, alongside Washington's own contested ``4E091`` "
"closed-weight rule ``[CN-A1]`` ``[US25]`` ``[GAO26]``."
msgstr ""
"**地平线之上（软件、模型权重与数据闸门）：** **2026 年 10 月 16 日** ，中国商务部与科技部联合发布 "
"**商务部与科技部2026年第48号公告** ，在人工智能与芯片（23 项）、生物医药（5 项）及光伏制造（12 项）三大领域提出 **40 "
"项技术管制点** 修订草案，并于当天下午同步启动强制性的出口前信息登记机制 ``[CN48]`` ``[CNQA]`` 。私下跨境转移突破 "
":math:`10^{26}` FLOPs 训练算力、 **2 万亿参数规模** 或位列 **全球前十评测榜单** 的前沿大模型核心技术（ "
"``266504X`` ），将被纳入出口许可闸门，与华盛顿自身充满法律拉锯的 ``4E091`` 闭源模型权重规则形成对映 ``[CN-A1]`` "
"``[US25]`` ``[GAO26]`` 。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:36
msgid ""
"Even if software licenses remain free on paper, open-source AI cannot "
"thrive in a vacuum: if export controls ration the chips needed to train "
"open models, lock up open silicon blueprints, or price local hardware out "
"of reach for hospitals and universities, humanity gets nudged back from "
"owning minds to renting metered corporate cloud windows."
msgstr ""
"哪怕软件许可证在纸面上依旧自由，开源人工智能也绝无可能在真空中繁茂生长：一旦出口管制配给甚至卡住训练开源模型所需的算力芯片、锁死开放芯片架构蓝图，或是让医院与大学再也买不起本地部署硬件，全人类就将在不知不觉间被推回老路：从真正拥有心智工具，退化为按量租用科技巨头的云端计费窗口。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:38
msgid "The Fortress Trap: Why High Walls Leave Everyone Worse Off"
msgstr "堡垒陷阱：为何筑起高墙反而让所有人受损"

#: ../../book/index.rst:41
msgid ""
"Every capital builds export walls hoping to stay ahead and stay safe. At "
"first glance, hoarding technology inside national borders sounds like "
"simple common sense: *if we keep our breakthroughs to ourselves, won't we "
"be stronger and safer?*"
msgstr ""
"每一座首都筑起出口高墙，初衷都是为了保持领先、守护安全。乍看之下，把核心技术严密留在国境之内似乎再合常理不过： *如果我们把重大突破留给自己独享，难道不会更强大、更安全吗？*"

#: ../../book/index.rst:43
msgid ""
"To test whether that instinct holds up in the real world, imagine two "
"technological neighbors across a dark strait, **Country A** and **Country "
"B**. Each country faces a basic choice over its non-military AI software "
"and chip designs:"
msgstr ""
"为了检验这种直觉在真实世界里是否站得住脚，不妨设想幽暗海峡两岸隔海相望的两个科技大国：**A 国** 与 **B 国** 。围绕各自的非军事人工智能软件与芯片设计，两国都面临着同样两种基础选择："

#: ../../book/index.rst:45
msgid ""
"**Share Openly (S):** Publish research papers, open-weight AI models, and "
"safety fixes so engineers, doctors, and universities everywhere can "
"inspect, test, and build upon them."
msgstr ""
"**公开共享 (S)：** 公开发表学术论文、开放权重人工智能模型与安全修复补丁，让全世界的工程师、临床医生与高校学者都能自由检视、测试，并在前人基础上继续创新。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:46
msgid ""
"**Build a Wall (W):** Lock AI models, chip blueprints, and computing "
"hardware behind broad export controls so outsiders cannot easily use or "
"inspect them."
msgstr ""
"**筑起高墙 (W)：** 用宽泛的出口管制将人工智能模型、芯片设计图纸与算力硬件封锁起来，令外界难以轻易获取、使用或审视它们。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:48
msgid ""
"Notice the catch: what happens to Country A depends not only on Country "
"A's own decision, but also on what Country B decides at the exact same "
"moment. Mathematicians and economists have a name for studying situations "
"like this. They call it **game theory**: not a study of board games, but "
"the clear math of strategic choices where everyone's outcome is tied "
"together."
msgstr ""
"请留意这里的关键转折：A 国最终处境如何，不仅取决于 A 国自己的选择，更取决于 B 国在同一时刻做出了什么选择。数学家与经济学家专门为研究这类互动情境起了一个名字，叫做 **博弈论** ：它并不是在研究棋牌游戏，而是用一清二楚的数学逻辑，剖析当各方命运彼此咬合时，不同战略抉择究竟会通向怎样的结局。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:52
msgid ""
"**Analytical model:** The plain-number score sheet and equations below "
"illustrate strategic incentives across open and closed technology "
"choices; they are an analytical proof rather than a legal rule."
msgstr "**分析模型说明：** 下文的通俗计分单与数学方程旨在直观展现开放与封闭技术抉择背后的结构性战略激励；它们属于数理分析证明，而非法定条文。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:57
msgid ""
"Two fortresses across a dark strait: when rival powers hoard dim, "
"solitary flames behind crimson battlements, storm shadows gather around "
"both, whereas two flames joined in a shared lighthouse illuminate the "
"entire sea."
msgstr ""
"隔着幽暗海峡对峙的两座堡垒：当竞争大国在深红垛口后各自死守微弱孤火，风暴的阴影便同时笼罩两岸；唯有两束火光汇入同一座共享灯塔，才能照亮整片浩瀚海域。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:59
msgid "Step 1: Keeping Score with Plain Everyday Numbers"
msgstr "第一步：用信封背面就能算清的日常数字来计分"

#: ../../book/index.rst:62
msgid ""
"Before touching a single equation, let us keep score on a simple "
"**20-point scale** that anyone can check on the back of an envelope:"
msgstr ""
"在写下任何一个数学公式之前，我们先用一套任何人拿张信封背面就能心算核对的 **20 分制日常账本** 来算一算得失："

#: ../../book/index.rst:64
msgid ""
"**Homegrown work (+10 points):** Working purely on its own, each "
"country's scientists, labs, and factories generate **+10** points of "
"baseline progress."
msgstr ""
"**本国基础研发（+10 分）：** 单靠本国科学家、实验室与工厂独立攻关，每个国家都能稳稳创造 **+10** 分的基础科技进步。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:65
msgid ""
"**The shared-knowledge bonus (+8 points):** Whenever a country chooses "
"**Share Openly (S)**, its published breakthroughs, open code, and bug "
"fixes save the other country years of dead ends, adding **+8** points to "
"the other side without taking a single point away from the sharer "
"(Jefferson's candle)."
msgstr ""
"**公开共享红利（+8 分）：** 只要一国选择 **公开共享 (S)** ，它发表的前沿突破、开源代码与漏洞补丁就能帮对方省去数年摸黑试错的弯路，为对方额外带来 **+8** 分红利，而分享者自己连一分都不会少（正如杰斐逊笔下那支点亮他人却不损自身光明的蜡烛）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:66
msgid ""
"**The duplicate-factory cost (-1 point):** Choosing **Build a Wall (W)** "
"forces a country to spend billions reinventing supply chains, chip tools, "
"and isolated computing clusters from scratch, costing **-1** point."
msgstr ""
"**重复建设成本（-1 分）：** 一旦选择 **筑起高墙 (W)** ，就不得不耗费巨资从头重复打造整条供应链、芯片制造工具与孤立算力集群，白白付出 **-1** 分的代价。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:67
msgid ""
"**The temporary one-sided lead (+5 or -5 points):** If *only one* country "
"builds a wall while the other keeps sharing, the walled country briefly "
"gets both worlds: it still reads the open country's discoveries (**+8**) "
"while keeping its own secret, grabbing a **+5** monopoly lead and pushing "
"the lone sharer **-5** behind. *Notice what happens if both build walls:* "
"neither can read the other's work, so the **+5** and **-5** cancel "
"straight back to **0**."
msgstr ""
"**短暂的单边领先差（+5 分或 -5 分）：** 倘若 *只有一国* 筑起高墙、而另一国继续公开共享，筑墙国便能在短期内两头占便宜：它既能照常阅读开放国的科研成果（ **+8** ），又把自己的技术锁进保险柜，从而抢到 **+5** 分的垄断领先，同时把独自开放的一方甩在身后承受 **-5** 分的滞后。 *但请留心当两国同时筑墙时会发生什么：* 谁也看不到对方的成果，那 **+5** 与 **-5** 当场互相抵消，直接归 **0** 。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:68
msgid ""
"**The hidden-bug danger (-1, -2, or -4 points):** Every complex AI model "
"or chip design can hide dangerous alignment flaws or security bugs. How "
"much harm those hidden bugs cause depends on how many independent eyes "
"are allowed to inspect the technology."
msgstr ""
"**暗藏漏洞的风险扣分（-1、-2 或 -4 分）：** 每一套复杂的人工智能大模型或芯片架构内部，都可能潜伏着危险的对齐失控隐患或高危安全漏洞。这些隐患最终会酿成多大祸患，直接取决于全世界有多少双独立的眼睛获准去审视和检验它。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:70
msgid ""
"Step 2: Why Secrecy Multiplies Danger Instead of Safety (The Coin-Flip "
"Test)"
msgstr "第二步：为何保密反而成倍放大危险？（抛硬币查漏洞直觉测试）"

#: ../../book/index.rst:73
msgid ""
"Why would locking AI behind high walls make the world *more* dangerous "
"rather than safer? Think of tossing a coin while hunting for a hidden "
"software bug."
msgstr ""
"把人工智能锁在高墙背后，怎么反而会让世界变得 *更加* 危险而不是更安全呢？不妨用日常“抛硬币找软件漏洞”的简单算术来想一想。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:75
msgid ""
"Suppose a serious flaw slips into a new AI model, and any single research "
"team testing behind closed doors has a **50 percent** (:math:`1/2`) "
"chance of missing it before launch:"
msgstr ""
"假设某款新大模型里悄悄混入了一处严重安全缺陷，任何一支关起门来内部自测的研发团队，在上线前都有 **50%** （ :math:`1/2` ）的概率不小心漏掉它："

#: ../../book/index.rst:77
msgid ""
"If **1 closed lab** checks the system in secret, there is a **50%** "
"chance the dangerous flaw survives unseen into the real world."
msgstr ""
"如果只有 **1 家封闭实验室** 关门秘密自查，这处致命隐患就有整整 **50%** 的概率漏网逃进现实世界。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:78
msgid ""
"If **4 independent teams** openly inspect and test the system, *all four* "
"would have to miss the flaw in a row: :math:`(1/2)^4 = \\mathbf{6.25\\%}`."
msgstr ""
"如果有 **4 支独立团队** 共同公开审视测试，必须 *四支团队接连全部看走眼* 才会漏掉它，漏检概率骤降至 :math:`(1/2)^4 = \\mathbf{6.25\\%}` 。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:79
msgid ""
"If **10 independent communities** around the world (universities, "
"hospital engineers, chip designers, security auditors) inspect it openly, "
"the chance that *every single one* misses the flaw drops to "
":math:`(1/2)^{10}`, **less than 0.1%** (under one in a thousand)."
msgstr ""
"如果全世界有 **10 个独立技术社区** （高校学者、医院信息工程师、芯片架构师、安全审计员）共同公开检验， *十组人马无一察觉* 的概率便暴跌至 :math:`(1/2)^{10}` ， **不足 0.1%** （不到千分之一）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:81
msgid ""
"Open-source engineers call this \"many-eyes\" discovery **Linus's Law** "
"(*\"given enough eyeballs, all bugs are shallow\"*). In mathematics, if a "
"hidden flaw starts with probability :math:`p_0` and each independent "
"auditing group catches it with probability :math:`q`, then across "
":math:`n` independent groups the chance that a dangerous flaw survives "
"unnoticed shrinks exponentially:"
msgstr ""
"开源软件工程师将这种“众人拾柴揪隐患”的规律称为 **莱纳斯定律（众目定律）** （ *“只要眼睛足够多，所有漏洞都无处遁形”* ）。用数学语言表达：假设某处隐藏缺陷出现的初始概率为 :math:`p_0` ，每个独立审计团队揪出它的概率为 :math:`q` ，那么经过全球 :math:`n` 个独立团队交叉检验后，危险漏洞依然漏网幸存的概率将呈指数级断崖下跌："

#: ../../book/index.rst:83
msgid "P(\\text{flaw survives}) = p_0 (1 - q)^n"
msgstr "P(\\text{flaw survives}) = p_0 (1 - q)^n"

#: ../../book/index.rst:87
msgid ""
"That simple curve explains why our hidden-bug penalty changes across the "
"board:"
msgstr "正是这条简洁而冷峻的指数曲线，解释了为何不同开放程度下的安全扣分截然不同："

#: ../../book/index.rst:89
msgid ""
"When **both countries share (S, S)**, global teams test weights and chip "
"tools in the open, while hospitals, power grids, and small cities can run "
"local open AI to defend their networks. Bug risk stays low (**R = 1**)."
msgstr ""
"当 **两国都选择公开共享 (S, S)** 时，全球科研团队在阳光下共同检验模型权重与芯片工具，医院、电网与中小城市也能在本地部署开源 AI 守卫自身网络安全，漏洞风险保持在最低水平（ **R = 1** ）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:90
msgid ""
"When **one country walls up (S, W or W, S)**, half of global scrutiny "
"disappears behind closed doors, doubling unseen risk (**R = 2**)."
msgstr ""
"当 **一国单边筑墙 (S, W 或 W, S)** 时，全球一半的独立审视力量消失在紧闭的大门之后，未知隐患风险随之翻倍（ **R = 2** ）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:91
msgid ""
"When **both countries wall up (W, W)**, three hazards stack together: "
"**(1)** closed black boxes have far fewer independent testers; **(2)** "
"everyday hospitals, schools, and utilities lose open defensive AI tools "
"while covert attackers ignore export laws anyway; and **(3)** rival "
"governments cannot see inside each other's secret labs, breeding "
"worst-case suspicion and rushed launches. Hidden danger quadruples (**R = "
"4**)."
msgstr ""
"当 **两国双双筑起高墙 (W, W)** 时，三重风险便会叠加引爆： **(1)** 封闭黑箱令外部独立测试的眼睛大幅减少； **(2)** 普通医院、学校与水电公共事业失去了开放权重的安全防御工具，而暗处的恶意攻击者本来就无视任何出口禁令； **(3)** 竞争大国看不见对方秘密实验室里的动向，极易滋生最坏猜忌并倒逼各方压缩安全测试仓促上线。潜伏的系统性风险由此暴增至四倍（ **R = 4** ）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:93
msgid "Step 3: Checking All Four Choices Side by Side"
msgstr "第三步：把四种组合并排放在一起算总账"

#: ../../book/index.rst:96
msgid ""
"Putting those five plain pieces together gives one transparent score rule "
"for either country:"
msgstr "把上面五项加减法拼在一起，就能得出适用于任一国家的透明总分公式："

#: ../../book/index.rst:98
msgid ""
"\\text{Net Score} = 10 + B_{\\text{share}} - C_{\\text{wall}} + "
"L_{\\text{solo}} - R_{\\text{bugs}}"
msgstr ""
"\\text{Net Score} = 10 + B_{\\text{share}} - C_{\\text{wall}} + "
"L_{\\text{solo}} - R_{\\text{bugs}}"

#: ../../book/index.rst:102
msgid ""
"where :math:`B_{\\text{share}} = 8` if the other side shares (else "
":math:`0`), :math:`C_{\\text{wall}} = 1` if you build a wall (else "
":math:`0`), :math:`L_{\\text{solo}} = +5` or :math:`-5` only when one "
"side walls alone (:math:`0` if both make the same choice), and "
":math:`R_{\\text{bugs}} \\in \\{1, 2, 4\\}`."
msgstr ""
"其中：只要对方选择共享，共享红利 :math:`B_{\\text{share}} = 8` （否则为 :math:`0` ）；只要本国筑墙，重复建设成本 :math:`C_{\\text{wall}} = 1` （否则为 :math:`0` ）；单边领先差 :math:`L_{\\text{solo}}` 仅在一方单独筑墙时取 :math:`+5` 或 :math:`-5` （双方选择相同时归 :math:`0` ）；漏洞风险扣分 :math:`R_{\\text{bugs}} \\in \\{1, 2, 4\\}` 。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:104
msgid ""
"Now check all four boxes in :numref:`fig-game-theory` using ordinary "
"addition and subtraction:"
msgstr ""
"现在，只需用最普通的加减法，就能逐一核对 :numref:`fig-game-theory` 里的四个方格："

#: ../../book/index.rst:106
msgid ""
"**Both Share Openly (S, S):** Each country earns :math:`10 + 8 - 1 = "
"\\mathbf{+17}`. Combined world progress reaches **34**, and bug risk "
"stays at its safest (**1x**)."
msgstr ""
"**双方公开共享 (S, S)：** 两国各自获得 :math:`10 + 8 - 1 = \\mathbf{+17}` 分。全球总收益高达 **34** 分，且漏洞风险保持在最安全的基准水平（ **1x** ）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:107
msgid ""
"**Country A Shares Alone, Country B Builds a Wall (S, W):** Country B "
"still reads A's open work (**+8**), pays **-1** for its wall, grabs the "
"**+5** solo lead, and faces **-2** bug risk, scoring :math:`10 + 8 - 1 + "
"5 - 2 = \\mathbf{+20}`. Country A drops to :math:`10 + 0 - 5 - 2 = "
"\\mathbf{+3}` (world total falls to **23**)."
msgstr ""
"**A 国单独共享、B 国筑起高墙 (S, W)：** B 国照看 A 国的开源成果（ **+8** ），付出筑墙成本（ **-1** ），抢占单边领先（ **+5** ），承担翻倍漏洞风险（ **-2** ），总分跃升至 :math:`10 + 8 - 1 + 5 - 2 = \\mathbf{+20}` ；而 A 国则跌落至 :math:`10 + 0 - 5 - 2 = \\mathbf{+3}` （全球总收益降至 **23** ）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:108
msgid ""
"**Country A Builds a Wall, Country B Shares Alone (W, S):** The exact "
"mirror image: Country A scores **+20** and Country B drops to **+3** "
"(world total **23**)."
msgstr ""
"**A 国筑起高墙、B 国单独共享 (W, S)：** 结果完全镜像反转，A 国得 **+20** 分，B 国跌至 **+3** 分（全球总收益同为 **23** ）。"

#: ../../book/index.rst:109
msgid ""
"**Both Build Walls (W, W):** Neither gets the **+8** shared bonus, both "
"pay **-1** for duplicate factories, their solo leads cancel to **0**, and "
"bug risk hits **-4**. Each country finishes with only :math:`10 + 0 - 1 + "
"0 - 4 = \\mathbf{+5}` (world total crashes to **10**)."
msgstr ""
"**双方都筑起高墙 (W, W)：** 谁也拿不到 **+8** 的共享红利，双方都要倒贴 **-1** 的重复建厂成本，单边领先优势抵消归 **0** ，漏洞风险扣分飙升至 **-4** 。最终两国各自只剩下可怜的 :math:`10 + 0 - 1 + 0 - 4 = \\mathbf{+5}` 分（全球总收益断崖暴跌至 **10** ）。"

